From 78ceaf7d229a8bbe937628734315c0b142de72c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:41:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(network): isolate forked socket ownership test

The fork-based procfs ownership test runs in the same libtest process as proxy tests. Its child inherits every socket open in that process, so parallel CONNECT tests can observe one inode under PIDs with different policy identities. The proxy correctly fails closed with policy_denied, making the test expect a 503 but receive a 403. Slower aarch64 scheduling and /proc scans expose the race reliably.

Move the fork scenario into a dedicated integration-test executable. It still verifies that both parent and child own the target socket, while process isolation prevents it from inheriting sockets created by unrelated tests. Register the new target with Bazel and keep parallel test execution enabled.

Signed-off-by: Robert Sturla <rsturla@redhat.com>
---
 .../openshell-supervisor-network/BUILD.bazel  | 12 +++
 .../src/procfs.rs                             | 68 ---------------
 .../tests/procfs_socket_ownership.rs          | 86 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 98 insertions(+), 68 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 crates/openshell-supervisor-network/tests/procfs_socket_ownership.rs

